From b69915edab2f76a04003a3f222f4200a580f5429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:25:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] input: CRT lightgun mode 1: take the aim from the game's
 flash

In many gun games the aim point is dark most of the time (about 82% of
the gun's reports in Point Blank saw no light) and the game flashes the
screen after the trigger so the gun can measure. The continuous tracker
then holds, expires, or throws the aim to the edge between shots.

LIGHTGUN_CRT_MODE=1 (default): on a trigger pull the pointer is set to the
tracker's estimate at that instant, then to the median of the first three
complete valid reports that follow (the flash, within LIGHTGUN_CRT_SHOT_MS,
now 400 ms; in Point Blank the light returns 50-100 ms after the pull), and
it then holds until the next pull. A pull with no light and no flash stays
offscreen. The core is given the held aim (crtgun_deliver) instead of the
gun's raw axes. LIGHTGUN_CRT_MODE=0 keeps the continuous tracker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
